# draft
// FIRST DRAFT (M7): rewrite or sign off. Voice: docs/voice.md. Flags: docs/story-drafts.md.
// The last scene before the ending. It changes nothing: the ending follows from the run.
EXTERNAL flag(name)
The sun doesn't set. It goes out, like a lamp someone has pinched.
The path is quiet at last. Down its whole length there's nobody left to judge, only the slates on your table, stacked higher than the clerk, and the ink drying on your stamps.
The ravens sit side by side on the end of the table. Muninn leans against Huginn, and Huginn lets him.
{
- flag("wood"):
  Somewhere in the hills there's a wood you've never seen. You think of dew on the leaves, and your family breathing quietly under the trees.
- flag("ferryman"):
  The grey boat is gone from the shingle below the gate. You don't know when it left. You didn't see anyone get in.
- flag("loki_deal"):
  In the north the sea is burning, and on it, very small at this distance, something with a rail is moving.
- flag("stay_home"):
  At home they'll have banked the fire high tonight. You can almost smell the peat.
- else:
  You think of home, and can't tell any more whether you're remembering it or making it up.
}
* [Put the stamp down.]
  You set it on the table face down, so it won't mark the wood.
* [Keep it in your hand.]
  You hold on to it. Someone might still come up the path. Someone always has.
- Far off, very faintly, you hear a wolf.
-> END
